#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Change the Wi-Fi hotspot's settings, scan for networks, forget a saved one, set the order of the saved ones, and
end or cancel the countdown of a Wi-Fi join.

tm-job-network.service runs this as root (`python -EP`), after tm-control writes the request
/run/tm-control/jobs/network.json, a JSON object of one of these forms:
- {"action": "hotspot"} plus any of "enabled", "name", "password", and "hidden", only the ones the admin sent: turn the
  hotspot on or off and change its name, its password, and whether its name is hidden;
- {"action": "scan"}: scan with `iw` and write the networks heard to SCAN_FILE in the run directory;
- {"action": "forget", "uuid": "<uuid>"}: delete one saved Wi-Fi network (a Wi-Fi client profile);
- {"action": "order", "uuids": ["<uuid>", ...]}: set the order the unit tries the saved networks in, first to last;
- {"action": "switch-now"} and {"action": "cancel"}: control tm-job-network-join, the job that tests a network and
  switches to it after a countdown.
tm-control runs unprivileged as the manifest's code owner, who owns /run/tm-control, so the request is treated as
hostile:
- the jobs directory is opened without following a symlink and must belong to the code owner and be writable by no
  one else; the request is opened and deleted relative to it, so its path can't be swapped mid-way;
- the request must be a small regular file of the code owner's with one link, holding a JSON object of exactly one of
  the forms above and nothing else. For hotspot, enabled and hidden must be booleans; the name and the password must
  match NAME_PATTERN and PASSWORD_PATTERN below as a whole (tm-control's own rules, which a test keeps the same), and
  the name must be at most NAME_MAX_BYTES bytes in UTF-8. A uuid must be a lowercase UUID as UUID_PATTERN says; order
  takes 1 to MAX_ORDER of them, none twice;
- every value goes to nmcli as one argument of an argv list, never through a shell;
- the secrets directory is opened without following a symlink and must belong to root and be writable by no one
  else. The password file is written to a new file in it (O_EXCL, 0640, root and the directory's group) and renamed
  over hotspot_password.
Trusted: the install manifest and the secrets directory (root's), the profile NetworkManager holds, and the lock file
and run directory in /run/traffic-monitor (root's). Not trusted: what `iw` prints. It is the names and settings of
other people's networks, heard from the air, so it is parsed as text (parse_scan), a name is data and never a path or a
command, nothing from it is printed, and it reaches nmcli only when tm-control sends it back in a later request.

One run, in order:
1. Read the manifest (the code owner, the Wi-Fi device, and the hotspot profile's name), then the request.
2. Check the request. A refusal names the rule, never a value.
3. Take the lock that tm-network-retry takes too (flock on LOCK, tried every half second for LOCK_WAIT seconds), so
   the timer never moves the radio in the middle of a change. Still held: refused.
4. Read the profile: autoconnect, name, hidden, key management, and, when the request has a password, the
   profile's (nmcli -s). No profile: refused.
5. Work out what differs. A password differs when it isn't the password file's, or isn't the profile's, or the
   profile isn't WPA2 personal (wpa-psk); it then sets the five WPA2 properties. Nothing differs: `nothing to change`.
6. A new password goes to the password file first, the old content kept in memory: the file is the source of truth.
7. One `nmcli connection modify` with every change. If it fails, the old password file is put back.
8. Then the first of these that applies: turned off, the hotspot is taken down if it is up; the name, password, or
   hidden setting changed on the profile and the hotspot is up, it restarts (`connection up` on the active profile
   applies them; a failed restart is tried once more, and counts when the device ends up on the hotspot);
   turned on, on the built-in radio only (never a USB adapter), the radio is switched on if it is off and the
   hotspot started if the radio is idle; a failed start still counts when NetworkManager brought the hotspot up by
   itself within UP_WAIT seconds, as it does when autoconnect is switched on while the radio is idle. Otherwise the
   change waits for the hotspot's next start.
It prints one line per thing done and exits 0, or exits 1 with `refused: <sentence>` or
`failed: <step> (<error type>)`, such as `(nmcli exit status 4)`, ending `; the settings are saved` once the profile
was changed.

The other three actions take the same lock, then:
- scan: refused unless the radio is built in (not a USB adapter) and switched on. Runs `iw dev <device> scan flush`,
  which empties the kernel's cache first (a plain scan keeps listing a network for about 30 s after it left the air).
  A non-zero exit (`iw` exits 240 while NetworkManager scans, as it does in the background on a network, and for 10 to
  14 s after the hotspot restarts) is tried again every SCAN_RETRY_WAIT seconds while SCAN_TIMEOUT seconds, all tries
  together, last; a try that hangs until the time is up is not tried again. A failure is `failed: scan (iw exit
  status N)` or `(iw timed out)` and leaves the old file. Otherwise SCAN_FILE is written under a temporary name and
  renamed, 0644: {"at": <ISO time, UTC>, "monotonic": <time.monotonic()>, "networks":
  [{"ssid", "signal" (0 to 100), "security" (open, password, wpa3, enterprise, or other)}]}, strongest first, at most
  MAX_NETWORKS. A network with no name is left out. Prints `heard N networks`.
- forget: the profile must be a Wi-Fi client (type 802-11-wireless, mode infrastructure), else refused, and it must
  exist. Deletes it by uuid. When the device was on it and the hotspot starts by itself, waits RETURN_WAIT seconds for
  the device to reach a connected state on another profile (right after the delete it can still read connected on the
  deleted one) and starts the hotspot if it didn't.
- order: the uuids must be exactly the Wi-Fi client profiles that start by themselves. The first gets
  connection.autoconnect-priority N (N is how many), the last 1; only profiles whose value differs are changed.

The join's two controls never wait for the lock, which the join job holds through its whole run. They read its state
file, JOIN_STATE_FILE in the run directory, and write a word to CONTROL_FILE beside it (under a temporary name and
renamed, 0644), which the join job reads every second:
- switch-now: when the stage is `countdown`, writes `switch` (`asked the join to switch now`); otherwise refused.
- cancel: no state file is refused. Otherwise the lock is tried once, without waiting, and the first that applies:
  the lock is held and the stage isn't final, so a join is running: writes `cancel` (`asked the join to cancel`). The
  stage is final: removes the state file and any control file (`cleared the result`). The lock is free and the stage
  isn't final, so the join died: holding the lock, rolls back any checkpoint NetworkManager still holds (busctl; the
  Checkpoints property, then CheckpointRollback on each), waits up to RETURN_WAIT seconds for the device to be
  connected, deletes the profile under test unless it is a saved network, then removes the state file and any
  control file (`cleared the result`). A rollback that fails is printed and the clean-up goes on.
  When the retry timer happens to hold the lock while a dead join's state is cancelled, the first case applies and
  nobody reads the control file; the next cancel, or the next join, clears it.

No password is ever printed: nmcli's error text is never quoted (it can carry the command line), an unexpected error
prints only its kind, and every password the job learns (the request's, the file's, the profile's) is still scrubbed
from each line it prints. The request is deleted
whatever happens, unless the jobs directory itself can't be trusted: when the manifest can't be read (so the code
owner who must own the directory is unknown), or the directory fails its owner and mode checks, the request is left
where it is, and tm-control clears a request no job is waiting for.

Standard library only, and no tm_control imports: this runs from the root-owned copy in
/usr/local/libexec/traffic-monitor/. TM_CONTROL_MANIFEST and TM_CONTROL_SECRETS_DIR name the manifest and the
secrets directory, as for tm-job-set-secret: its root-owned unit sets both. Tests pass the request path as argv[1], set
those two, and set NMCLI, IW, BUSCTL, TM_SYS_NET, TM_NETWORK_LOCK, TM_NETWORK_LOCK_WAIT, TM_NETWORK_RUN_DIR,
TM_NETWORK_RETURN_WAIT, TM_NETWORK_SCAN_RETRY_WAIT, and TM_NETWORK_SCAN_TIMEOUT, which are ignored when running as
root. Run as anyone but root (tests only), the secrets directory may be that user's instead of root's.
"""

import datetime
import fcntl
import json
import os
import pwd
import re
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import time

REQUEST = "/run/tm-control/jobs/network.json"
MANIFEST = "/etc/traffic-monitor/manifest.json"
SECRETS_DIR = "/etc/traffic-monitor/secrets"
NMCLI = "/usr/bin/nmcli"
IW = "/usr/sbin/iw"
BUSCTL = "/usr/bin/busctl"
SYS_NET = "/sys/class/net"
RUN_DIR = "/run/traffic-monitor"
LOCK = "/run/traffic-monitor/network.lock"
LOCK_WAIT = 10  # seconds
SCAN_FILE = "network-scan.json"
JOIN_STATE_FILE = "network-join.json"  # the join job's state
CONTROL_FILE = "network-join.control"  # a word for the join job: switch or cancel
SCAN_TIMEOUT = 60  # seconds for a scan, all its tries together
SCAN_RETRY_WAIT = 5  # seconds between the tries of a scan that failed (iw is busy for about 15 s after a hotspot change)
RETURN_WAIT = 15  # seconds for NetworkManager to bring the Wi-Fi back by itself after a network is forgotten
MAX_NETWORKS = 100  # networks kept from a scan
MAX_ORDER = 64  # networks in one order
UP_WAIT = 30  # seconds: nmcli --wait for a start, and how long a failed start may take to come up by itself
PASSWORD_FILE = "hotspot_password"
MAX_REQUEST = 4096  # bytes
MAX_PASSWORD_FILE = 1024  # bytes
FIELDS = ("enabled", "name", "password", "hidden")
ACTIONS = ("hotspot", "scan", "forget", "order", "switch-now", "cancel")
FINAL = ("joined", "failed", "cancelled", "switch_failed")  # the join's stages that end it
UUID_PATTERN = r"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}"

# tm-control's rules (modules/network/router.py); a test keeps the two the same.
NAME_MAX_BYTES = 32
NAME_PATTERN = r"[^\x00-\x20\x7f](?:[^\x00-\x1f\x7f]*[^\x00-\x20\x7f])?"  # no control characters or edge spaces
PASSWORD_PATTERN = r"[\x21-\x7e][\x20-\x7e]{6,61}[\x21-\x7e]"  # 8 to 63 printable ASCII

WIFI = "802-11-wireless"
SECURITY = "802-11-wireless-security"
WPA2 = [(f"{SECURITY}.key-mgmt", "wpa-psk"), (f"{SECURITY}.proto", "rsn"), (f"{SECURITY}.pairwise", "ccmp"),
        (f"{SECURITY}.group", "ccmp")]
NM = ("org.freedesktop.NetworkManager", "/org/freedesktop/NetworkManager", "org.freedesktop.NetworkManager")
NM_PATH = r"/org/freedesktop/NetworkManager/[A-Za-z0-9_/]+"
CONNECTED = 100  # NetworkManager's device states
JOINING = range(40, 100)


class Refused(Exception):
    """The request can't be carried out. The message says why and never holds a value from the request."""


class NmcliFailed(Exception):
    """nmcli failed or timed out. The message has a fixed form (exit status, timeout); nmcli's output is never quoted."""


class BusctlFailed(NmcliFailed):
    """busctl failed or timed out. The message has a fixed form; busctl's output is never quoted."""


class IwFailed(NmcliFailed):
    """iw failed or timed out. The message has a fixed form; iw's output is never quoted."""

    def __init__(self, message, timed_out=False):
        super().__init__(message)
        self.timed_out = timed_out


def trusted(name, default):
    """The setting `name` from the environment, but only when not root: root always uses the installed values."""
    return default if os.geteuid() == 0 else os.environ.get(name) or default


def trusted_seconds(name, default):
    """The number of seconds in the environment variable `name` (not root only), else `default`."""
    try:
        return float(trusted(name, str(default)))
    except ValueError:
        return float(default)


def manifest_path():
    """The manifest, from TM_CONTROL_MANIFEST (which the unit sets) or MANIFEST."""
    return os.environ.get("TM_CONTROL_MANIFEST") or MANIFEST


def secrets_dir_path():
    """The secrets directory, from TM_CONTROL_SECRETS_DIR (which the unit sets) or SECRETS_DIR."""
    return os.environ.get("TM_CONTROL_SECRETS_DIR") or SECRETS_DIR


def read_manifest(path):
    """The code owner's uid, the Wi-Fi device, and the hotspot profile's name, from the install manifest."""
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as file:
            manifest = json.load(file)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        raise Refused(f"the manifest {path} can't be read") from None
    if not isinstance(manifest, dict):
        raise Refused(f"the manifest {path} is not a JSON object")
    try:
        owner_uid = pwd.getpwnam(manifest.get("codeowner")).pw_uid
    except (KeyError, TypeError):
        raise Refused(f"the manifest {path} names no code owner that exists here") from None
    network = manifest.get("network", {})
    if not isinstance(network, dict):
        raise Refused(f"the manifest {path} has a network entry that is not a JSON object")
    device, profile = network.get("wifi_device", "wlan0"), network.get("hotspot_profile", "tm-hotspot")
    if not isinstance(device, str) or not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,14}", device):
        raise Refused(f"the manifest {path} names no usable Wi-Fi device")
    if not isinstance(profile, str) or not profile or profile.startswith("-") or "\x00" in profile:
        raise Refused(f"the manifest {path} names no usable hotspot profile")
    return owner_uid, device, profile


def open_jobs_dir(path, owner_uid):
    """A descriptor for the jobs directory, which must be the code owner's and writable by no one else."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError as error:
        raise Refused(f"the jobs directory can't be opened ({error.strerror})") from None
    info = os.fstat(fd)
    if info.st_uid != owner_uid or info.st_mode & 0o022:
        os.close(fd)
        raise Refused("the jobs directory is not tm-control's own")
    return fd


def read_request(dir_fd, name, owner_uid):
    """The request's JSON object, read without following a symlink and only from a small regular file."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=dir_fd)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise Refused("there is no request") from None
    except OSError as error:
        raise Refused(f"the request can't be opened ({error.strerror})") from None
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as file:
        info = os.fstat(file.fileno())
        if not stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode) or info.st_nlink != 1 or info.st_uid != owner_uid:
            raise Refused("the request is not a plain file of tm-control's")
        data = file.read(MAX_REQUEST + 1)
    if len(data) > MAX_REQUEST:
        raise Refused(f"the request is larger than {MAX_REQUEST} bytes")
    try:
        request = json.loads(data)
    except ValueError:
        raise Refused("the request is not JSON") from None
    if not isinstance(request, dict):
        raise Refused("the request is not a JSON object")
    return request


def valid_name(name):
    if not isinstance(name, str) or re.fullmatch(NAME_PATTERN, name) is None:
        return False
    try:
        return len(name.encode("utf-8")) <= NAME_MAX_BYTES
    except UnicodeEncodeError:  # a lone surrogate, which JSON can carry
        return False


def valid_uuid(value):
    return isinstance(value, str) and re.fullmatch(UUID_PATTERN, value) is not None


def check(request):
    """(the action, its values) once the request passes every rule: for hotspot the change as {field: value}, for scan
    {}, for forget {"uuid"}, for order {"uuids"}. No value is quoted in a refusal."""
    action = request.get("action")
    if action not in ACTIONS:
        raise Refused(f"the action must be {', '.join(ACTIONS[:-1])}, or {ACTIONS[-1]}")
    values = {key: value for key, value in request.items() if key != "action"}
    if action in ("scan", "switch-now", "cancel"):
        if values:
            raise Refused(f"a {action} request has the action and nothing else")
    elif action == "forget":
        if set(values) != {"uuid"} or not valid_uuid(values["uuid"]):
            raise Refused("a forget request has the action and a uuid, and nothing else")
    elif action == "order":
        uuids = values.get("uuids")
        if (set(values) != {"uuids"} or not isinstance(uuids, list) or not 1 <= len(uuids) <= MAX_ORDER
                or not all(valid_uuid(item) for item in uuids) or len(set(uuids)) != len(uuids)):
            raise Refused(f"an order request has the action and 1 to {MAX_ORDER} different uuids, and nothing else")
    else:
        check_hotspot(values)
    return action, values


def check_hotspot(change):
    """Refuse a hotspot change that is empty, has other fields, or holds a value outside its rule."""
    if not change or not set(change) <= set(FIELDS):
        raise Refused(f"the request must have the action and one or more of {', '.join(FIELDS)}, and nothing else")
    for key in ("enabled", "hidden"):
        if key in change and not isinstance(change[key], bool):
            raise Refused("enabled and hidden must be true or false")
    if "name" in change and not valid_name(change["name"]):
        raise Refused(f"the name must be 1 to {NAME_MAX_BYTES} bytes, with no control characters and no space at "
                      "either end")
    if "password" in change and (not isinstance(change["password"], str)
                                 or re.fullmatch(PASSWORD_PATTERN, change["password"]) is None):
        raise Refused("the password must be 8 to 63 printable ASCII characters, with no space at either end")


def take_lock(path, wait):
    """A descriptor holding flock(LOCK_EX) on path, or Refused after trying every half second for `wait` seconds.

    The lock's directory is made when missing (0755). Closing the descriptor, or the end of the process, frees it."""
    directory = os.path.dirname(path)
    if directory:
        os.makedirs(directory, mode=0o755, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o644)
    deadline = time.monotonic() + wait
    while True:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            return fd
        except BlockingIOError:
            remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
            if remaining <= 0:
                os.close(fd)
                raise Refused("the unit is trying a saved network right now; try again in a minute") from None
            time.sleep(min(0.5, remaining))


def unescape(value):
    """A value as nmcli -t and -g print it: a backslash escapes the character after it (`:` and `\\`)."""
    out, escaped = [], False
    for char in value:
        if char == "\\" and not escaped:
            escaped = True
        else:
            out.append(char)
            escaped = False
    return "".join(out)


def split_terse(line):
    """The unescaped fields of one nmcli -t line, split at the colons that aren't escaped."""
    fields, current, escaped = [], [], False
    for char in line:
        if escaped:
            current.append(char)
            escaped = False
        elif char == "\\":
            escaped = True
        elif char == ":":
            fields.append("".join(current))
            current = []
        else:
            current.append(char)
    fields.append("".join(current))
    return fields


class Nmcli:
    """Runs nmcli. Every password it was told about is scrubbed from what this script prints."""

    def __init__(self, binary):
        self.binary = binary
        self.hidden = set()
        self.last_error = ""

    def hide(self, *values):
        """Hide each value, and the form nmcli's terse output escapes it to."""
        for value in values:
            if value:
                self.hidden.add(value)
                self.hidden.add(value.replace("\\", "\\\\").replace(":", "\\:"))

    def scrub(self, text):
        for value in sorted(self.hidden, key=len, reverse=True):  # the longest first, so no part of one is left
            text = text.replace(value, "[hidden]")
        return text

    def call(self, *args, timeout=60):
        """(exit status, stdout). A command that outlives timeout is NmcliFailed."""
        try:
            result = subprocess.run(
                [self.binary, *args],
                capture_output=True,
                stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                env={**os.environ, "LC_ALL": "C.UTF-8"},  # yes and no, not a translation
                timeout=timeout,
                check=False,
            )
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            raise NmcliFailed(f"nmcli timed out after {timeout} s") from None
        if result.returncode != 0:  # its stderr is never quoted: it can carry the command line
            self.last_error = f"nmcli exit status {result.returncode}"
        return result.returncode, result.stdout.decode("utf-8", errors="replace")

    def run(self, *args, timeout=60):
        status, out = self.call(*args, timeout=timeout)
        if status != 0:
            raise NmcliFailed(self.last_error)
        return out

    def get(self, profile, prop, reveal=False):
        """One property of the profile, unescaped; "" when nmcli leaves its line out (a setting the profile lacks)."""
        status, out = self.call(*(["-s"] if reveal else []), "-g", prop, "connection", "show", "id", profile)
        if status == 10:  # nmcli: the connection doesn't exist
            raise Refused("there is no hotspot profile; run the installer")
        if status != 0:
            raise NmcliFailed(self.last_error)
        lines = out.split("\n")[:-1] if out.endswith("\n") else out.split("\n")
        if len(lines) > 1:
            raise NmcliFailed("nmcli answered with an unexpected number of lines")
        return unescape(lines[0]) if lines else ""

    def get_uuid(self, uuid, prop):
        """One property of the profile with that uuid, unescaped; None when there is no such profile."""
        status, out = self.call("-g", prop, "connection", "show", "uuid", uuid)
        if status == 10:  # nmcli: the connection doesn't exist
            return None
        if status != 0:
            raise NmcliFailed(self.last_error)
        lines = out.split("\n")[:-1] if out.endswith("\n") else out.split("\n")
        if len(lines) > 1:
            raise NmcliFailed("nmcli answered with an unexpected number of lines")
        return unescape(lines[0]) if lines else ""

    def device_uuid(self, device):
        """The uuid of the profile the device is on, or None."""
        out = self.run("-t", "-f", "GENERAL.CON-UUID", "device", "show", device)
        fields = split_terse(out.splitlines()[0]) if out.strip() else [""]
        value = fields[-1] if len(fields) > 1 else ""
        return value if re.fullmatch(UUID_PATTERN, value) else None

    def device(self, device):
        """(state number, the name of its profile or None) for the device."""
        values = {}
        for line in self.run("-t", "-f", "GENERAL.STATE,GENERAL.CONNECTION", "device", "show", device).splitlines():
            key, value = split_terse(line)[:2] if ":" in line else (line, "")
            values[key] = value
        state = re.match(r"\d+", values.get("GENERAL.STATE", ""))
        connection = values.get("GENERAL.CONNECTION", "")
        return int(state.group()) if state else 0, None if connection in ("", "--") else connection


def builtin_radio(device):
    """Whether the device is a Wi-Fi radio that is part of the unit, not a USB adapter (nor no radio at all)."""
    base = os.path.join(trusted("TM_SYS_NET", SYS_NET), device)
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(base, "wireless")):
        return False
    return not os.path.realpath(os.path.join(base, "device", "subsystem")).endswith("/usb")


def parse_scan(text):
    """The networks in the text `iw dev <device> scan` prints, strongest first: [{"ssid", "signal", "security"}].

    A network starts at a line that begins `BSS `. Its name is the first `SSID: ` line, with the bytes iw can't print
    (`\\xNN`) decoded as tm-network-retry does; a network with no such line (iw prints none for a hidden one), an empty
    name, or a name of only NUL bytes is left out. The signal, `-52.00 dBm`, becomes 0 to 100 (2 * (dBm + 100)), or 0
    when the block has none. The security is `password` when an `Authentication suites:` line under `RSN:` or `WPA:`
    names a suite containing PSK, else `wpa3` for SAE, else `enterprise` for 802.1X, else `other` when the capabilities
    include Privacy or any suite is listed, else `open`. Several access points with one name count once, with the
    strongest signal, and as `password` when any of them is. At most MAX_NETWORKS are returned."""
    blocks, current = [], None
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("BSS "):
            current = []
            blocks.append(current)
        elif current is not None:
            current.append(line)
    found = {}
    for lines in blocks:
        name = signal = None
        indents = [len(line) - len(line.lstrip()) for line in lines if line.strip()]
        top = min(indents) if indents else 0
        section, suites, privacy = "", [], False
        for line in lines:
            content = line.lstrip()
            if not content:
                continue
            if len(line) - len(content) <= top:  # a line of the block itself, which may open a section
                section = content.split(":", 1)[0]
                if name is None and content.startswith("SSID: "):
                    name = decode_name(content[len("SSID: "):])
                elif signal is None and (match := re.match(r"signal:\s*(-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?)\s*dBm", content)):
                    signal = max(0, min(100, 2 * (round(float(match.group(1))) + 100)))
                elif content.startswith("capability:"):
                    privacy = "Privacy" in content.split()
            if section in ("RSN", "WPA") and "Authentication suites:" in content:
                suites.append(content.split("Authentication suites:", 1)[1])
        if not name or not name.strip("\x00"):
            continue
        listed = " ".join(suites)
        if "PSK" in listed:
            security = "password"
        elif "SAE" in listed:
            security = "wpa3"
        elif "802.1X" in listed:
            security = "enterprise"
        elif privacy or listed.strip():
            security = "other"
        else:
            security = "open"
        signal = signal or 0
        seen = found.setdefault(name, {"ssid": name, "signal": signal, "security": security})
        was_password = seen["security"] == "password"
        if signal > seen["signal"]:
            seen.update(signal=signal, security=security)
        if was_password or security == "password":
            seen["security"] = "password"
    networks = sorted(found.values(), key=lambda network: -network["signal"])  # stable: ties keep the order heard
    return networks[:MAX_NETWORKS]


def decode_name(raw):
    """A name as iw prints it: `\\xNN` for a byte it can't print, decoded as UTF-8 when the bytes are valid."""
    raw = re.sub(r"\\x([0-9a-fA-F]{2})", lambda match: chr(int(match.group(1), 16)), raw)
    try:
        return raw.encode("latin-1").decode("utf-8")
    except UnicodeError:
        return raw


def run_iw(iw, device, timeout):
    """iw's scan output for the device, after a flush of the kernel's cache. A non-zero exit or a timeout is
    IwFailed, with a fixed message."""
    try:
        result = subprocess.run([iw, "dev", device, "scan", "flush"], capture_output=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                env={**os.environ, "LC_ALL": "C.UTF-8"}, timeout=timeout, check=False)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise IwFailed("iw timed out", timed_out=True) from None
    if result.returncode != 0:  # its stderr is never quoted
        raise IwFailed(f"iw exit status {result.returncode}")
    return result.stdout.decode("utf-8", errors="replace")


def write_scan(directory, networks):
    """SCAN_FILE in the run directory."""
    document = {"at": datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
                "monotonic": time.monotonic(), "networks": networks}
    write_run_file(directory, SCAN_FILE, json.dumps(document))


def write_run_file(directory, name, text):
    """A file in the run directory, written under a temporary name and renamed, 0644."""
    os.makedirs(directory, mode=0o755, exist_ok=True)
    final = os.path.join(directory, name)
    temporary = os.path.join(directory, f".{name}.{os.getpid()}.tmp")
    try:
        fd = os.open(temporary, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, 0o644)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as file:
            os.fchmod(file.fileno(), 0o644)
            file.write(text)
        os.rename(temporary, final)
    except BaseException:
        try:
            os.unlink(temporary)
        except OSError:
            pass
        raise


def read_join_state(directory):
    """The join job's state, a JSON object, or None when there is none or it is not one."""
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(directory, JOIN_STATE_FILE), encoding="utf-8") as file:
            state = json.load(file)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return state if isinstance(state, dict) else None


def remove_run_file(directory, name):
    try:
        os.unlink(os.path.join(directory, name))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass


def busctl(*args):
    """The `data` of busctl's `--json=short` answer. A failure is BusctlFailed; busctl's stderr is never read."""
    try:
        result = subprocess.run([trusted("BUSCTL", BUSCTL), "--system", "--json=short", *args], stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                                env={**os.environ, "LC_ALL": "C.UTF-8"}, timeout=30, check=False)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise BusctlFailed("busctl timed out") from None
    if result.returncode != 0:
        raise BusctlFailed(f"busctl exit status {result.returncode}")
    try:
        return json.loads(result.stdout)["data"]
    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        raise BusctlFailed("busctl answered in a form this script doesn't know") from None


def checkpoints():
    """The checkpoints NetworkManager holds now."""
    data = busctl("get-property", *NM, "Checkpoints")
    if not isinstance(data, list) or not all(isinstance(path, str) and re.fullmatch(NM_PATH, path) for path in data):
        raise BusctlFailed("busctl answered in a form this script doesn't know")
    return data


def plural(count, word):
    return f"{count} {word}" if count == 1 else f"{count} {word}s"


def read_profile(nm, profile, with_password):
    """The profile's settings this job may change; the password (hidden from then on) only when `with_password`."""
    current = {
        "enabled": nm.get(profile, "connection.autoconnect") == "yes",
        "name": nm.get(profile, f"{WIFI}.ssid"),
        "hidden": nm.get(profile, f"{WIFI}.hidden") == "yes",
        "key_mgmt": nm.get(profile, f"{SECURITY}.key-mgmt"),
        "password": None,
    }
    if with_password:
        current["password"] = nm.get(profile, f"{SECURITY}.psk", reveal=True)
        nm.hide(current["password"])
    return current


def differences(change, current, stored):
    """(the (property, value) pairs that make the profile what the change asks for, the fields that differ, whether
    the name, password, or hidden setting changes on the profile). `stored` is the password file's text or None.

    A password the profile already has but the file doesn't is written to the file and set again on the profile,
    which changes nothing there, so it alone restarts nothing."""
    pairs, fields, on_air = [], [], False
    if "enabled" in change and change["enabled"] != current["enabled"]:
        pairs.append(("connection.autoconnect", "yes" if change["enabled"] else "no"))
        fields.append("enabled")
    if "name" in change and change["name"] != current["name"]:
        pairs.append((f"{WIFI}.ssid", change["name"]))
        fields.append("name")
        on_air = True
    if "hidden" in change and change["hidden"] != current["hidden"]:
        pairs.append((f"{WIFI}.hidden", "yes" if change["hidden"] else "no"))
        fields.append("hidden")
        on_air = True
    if "password" in change:
        profile_differs = change["password"] != current["password"] or current["key_mgmt"] != "wpa-psk"
        if profile_differs or change["password"] != stored:
            pairs += [*WPA2, (f"{SECURITY}.psk", change["password"])]
            fields.append("password")
            on_air = on_air or profile_differs
    return pairs, fields, on_air


def open_secrets_dir(path):
    """A descriptor for the secrets directory: root's (as root) and writable by no one else."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError as error:
        raise Refused(f"the secrets directory can't be opened ({error.strerror})") from None
    info = os.fstat(fd)
    owner = 0 if os.geteuid() == 0 else os.getuid()  # tests run as themselves; on a device this is always root
    if info.st_uid != owner or info.st_mode & 0o022:
        os.close(fd)
        raise Refused("the secrets directory is not root's alone")
    return fd


def read_password_file(dir_fd):
    """The password file's bytes, or None when there is none."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(PASSWORD_FILE, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=dir_fd)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except OSError as error:
        raise Refused(f"the password file can't be read ({error.strerror})") from None
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as file:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(file.fileno()).st_mode):
            raise Refused("the password file is not a plain file")
        data = file.read(MAX_PASSWORD_FILE + 1)
    if len(data) > MAX_PASSWORD_FILE:
        raise Refused("the password file is too large")
    return data


def _temporary(dir_fd, name, mode):
    """A new file beside name in dir_fd, created O_EXCL so nothing that was there is ever opened."""
    for attempt in range(100):
        temporary = f".{name}.{os.getpid()}.{attempt}.tmp"
        try:
            fd = os.open(
                temporary,
                os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC,
                mode,
                dir_fd=dir_fd,
            )
        except FileExistsError:
            continue
        return temporary, fd
    raise FileExistsError("no free temporary name")


def _replace(dir_fd, name, data, mode, uid, gid):
    """Write data to a temporary file in dir_fd with mode, uid, and gid, then rename it over name."""
    temporary, fd = _temporary(dir_fd, name, 0o600)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as file:
            file.write(data)
            file.flush()
            os.fchmod(file.fileno(), mode)
            if uid is not None:
                os.fchown(file.fileno(), uid, gid)
            os.fsync(file.fileno())
        os.replace(temporary, name, src_dir_fd=dir_fd, dst_dir_fd=dir_fd)
    except BaseException:
        try:
            os.unlink(temporary, dir_fd=dir_fd)
        except OSError:
            pass
        raise
    os.fsync(dir_fd)


def write_password_file(dir_fd, data):
    """The password file holds data (no line end, as tm-hotspot-setup writes it); 0640, root and the directory's
    group. None removes the file, which is how a file that wasn't there before is put back."""
    if data is None:
        try:
            os.unlink(PASSWORD_FILE, dir_fd=dir_fd)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
        os.fsync(dir_fd)
        return
    owner = (0, os.fstat(dir_fd).st_gid) if os.geteuid() == 0 else (None, None)
    _replace(dir_fd, PASSWORD_FILE, data, 0o640, *owner)


def delete_request(dir_fd, name):
    try:
        os.unlink(name, dir_fd=dir_fd)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    except OSError as error:
        print(f"the request could not be deleted ({error.strerror})")


class Run:
    """One run's steps after the request passed its checks. `step` names what is under way, for a failure line."""

    def __init__(self, nm, device, profile):
        self.nm, self.device, self.profile = nm, device, profile
        self.step = "read the profile"
        self.saved = False
        self.saved_note = "; the settings are saved"
        self.secrets_fd = None

    def hotspot(self, change):
        nm = self.nm
        current = read_profile(nm, self.profile, "password" in change)
        old = stored = None
        if "password" in change:
            self.step = "read the password file"
            self.secrets_fd = open_secrets_dir(secrets_dir_path())
            old = read_password_file(self.secrets_fd)
            stored = old.decode("utf-8", errors="replace").rstrip("\r\n") if old is not None else None
            nm.hide(stored)
        pairs, fields, on_air = differences(change, current, stored)
        if not pairs:
            print("nothing to change")
            return

        if "password" in fields:
            self.step = "write the password file"
            write_password_file(self.secrets_fd, change["password"].encode())
            print("wrote the password file")

        self.step = "change the profile"
        try:
            nm.run("connection", "modify", "id", self.profile, *(word for pair in pairs for word in pair))
        except Exception:
            if "password" in fields:
                try:
                    write_password_file(self.secrets_fd, old)
                    print("put the password file back")
                except Exception as error:
                    print(f"failed: put the password file back ({type(error).__name__})")
            raise
        self.saved = True
        print(f"changed the profile ({', '.join(fields)})")

        self.step = "read the Wi-Fi device"
        _, connection = nm.device(self.device)
        up = connection == self.profile
        if change.get("enabled") is False and "enabled" in fields:
            if up:
                self.step = "take the hotspot down"
                nm.run("connection", "down", "id", self.profile, timeout=UP_WAIT + 30)
            print("turned the hotspot off")
        elif up and on_air:
            self.restart()
        elif change.get("enabled") is True and "enabled" in fields and builtin_radio(self.device):
            self.turn_on()
        else:
            print("saved; the change applies when the hotspot next starts")

    def scan(self):
        """Scan, and write what was heard. The old file stays when the scan fails."""
        self.step = "check the radio"
        if not builtin_radio(self.device):
            raise Refused("the unit has no built-in Wi-Fi radio")
        if self.nm.run("radio", "wifi").strip() != "enabled":
            raise Refused("the Wi-Fi radio is switched off")
        self.step = "scan"
        iw, limit = trusted("IW", IW), trusted_seconds("TM_NETWORK_SCAN_TIMEOUT", SCAN_TIMEOUT)
        wait = trusted_seconds("TM_NETWORK_SCAN_RETRY_WAIT", SCAN_RETRY_WAIT)
        started = time.monotonic()
        while True:
            try:
                text = run_iw(iw, self.device, limit - (time.monotonic() - started))
                break
            except IwFailed as error:
                # a try that hung used up the time; a busy iw is tried again while the time lasts
                if error.timed_out or limit - (time.monotonic() - started) - wait <= 0:
                    raise
                time.sleep(wait)
        networks = parse_scan(text)
        write_scan(trusted("TM_NETWORK_RUN_DIR", RUN_DIR), networks)
        print(f"heard {plural(len(networks), 'network')}")

    def forget(self, uuid):
        """Delete one saved Wi-Fi network, and see that the radio isn't left on nothing when it was on that one."""
        nm = self.nm
        self.step = "read the network"
        kind = nm.get_uuid(uuid, "connection.type")
        if kind is None:
            raise Refused("that network isn't saved any more")
        if kind != WIFI or nm.get_uuid(uuid, f"{WIFI}.mode") != "infrastructure":
            raise Refused("only a saved Wi-Fi network can be forgotten")
        in_use = nm.device_uuid(self.device) == uuid
        starts = in_use and nm.get(self.profile, "connection.autoconnect") == "yes"
        self.step = "forget the network"
        nm.run("connection", "delete", "uuid", uuid)
        self.saved, self.saved_note = True, "; the network is forgotten"
        print("forgot the network")
        if not in_use:
            return
        if not starts:
            print("the hotspot is off, so the Wi-Fi is idle")
            return
        self.step = "start the hotspot"
        wait = trusted_seconds("TM_NETWORK_RETURN_WAIT", RETURN_WAIT)
        deadline = time.monotonic() + wait
        # NetworkManager brings the hotspot up by itself, mostly. Right after the delete the device can still read
        # connected on the deleted profile, so the wait ends only on another one.
        while nm.device(self.device)[0] != CONNECTED or nm.device_uuid(self.device) == uuid:
            remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
            if remaining <= 0:
                nm.run("--wait", str(UP_WAIT), "connection", "up", "id", self.profile, timeout=UP_WAIT + 30)
                break
            time.sleep(min(0.5, remaining))
        print("started the hotspot" if nm.device(self.device)[1] == self.profile
              else "the unit moved to another saved network")

    def order(self, uuids):
        """Give the saved networks priorities from the count down to 1, in the order sent."""
        nm = self.nm
        self.step = "read the saved networks"
        current = {}
        for line in nm.run("-t", "-f", "UUID,TYPE,AUTOCONNECT", "connection", "show").splitlines():
            fields = split_terse(line)
            if len(fields) == 3 and fields[1] == WIFI and fields[2] == "yes":
                lines = nm.run("-g", f"{WIFI}.mode,connection.autoconnect-priority", "connection", "show", "uuid",
                               fields[0]).split("\n")
                if lines[0] == "infrastructure":
                    priority = lines[1] if len(lines) > 1 else ""
                    current[fields[0]] = int(priority) if re.fullmatch(r"-?\d+", priority) else 0
        if set(current) != set(uuids):
            raise Refused("the saved networks changed; reload the page")
        self.step = "set the order"
        changed = 0
        for index, uuid in enumerate(uuids):
            wanted = len(uuids) - index
            if current[uuid] != wanted:
                nm.run("connection", "modify", "uuid", uuid, "connection.autoconnect-priority", str(wanted))
                self.saved, self.saved_note = True, "; the order is partly set"
                changed += 1
        print(f"ordered {plural(len(uuids), 'network')}" if changed else "nothing to change")

    def switch_now(self):
        """Ask the join job to end its countdown now."""
        self.step = "switch now"
        run_dir = trusted("TM_NETWORK_RUN_DIR", RUN_DIR)
        state = read_join_state(run_dir)
        if state is None or state.get("stage") != "countdown":
            raise Refused("there is no countdown to end")
        write_run_file(run_dir, CONTROL_FILE, "switch")
        print("asked the join to switch now")

    def cancel(self):
        """Ask a running join to cancel, or clear what a finished or dead one left. The lock is tried once."""
        self.step = "cancel"
        run_dir = trusted("TM_NETWORK_RUN_DIR", RUN_DIR)
        try:
            lock_fd = take_lock(trusted("TM_NETWORK_LOCK", LOCK), 0)
        except Refused:
            lock_fd = None
        try:
            state = read_join_state(run_dir)
            if state is None:
                raise Refused("there is nothing to cancel")
            final = state.get("stage") in FINAL
            if lock_fd is None and not final:
                write_run_file(run_dir, CONTROL_FILE, "cancel")
                print("asked the join to cancel")
                return
            if not final:
                self.clear_dead_join(state)
            remove_run_file(run_dir, JOIN_STATE_FILE)
            remove_run_file(run_dir, CONTROL_FILE)
            print("cleared the result")
        finally:
            if lock_fd is not None:
                os.close(lock_fd)

    def clear_dead_join(self, state):
        """A join that died: roll back a checkpoint it left, wait for the radio, and delete its profile unless saved."""
        try:
            pending = checkpoints()
        except BusctlFailed as error:
            print(f"the checkpoints could not be read ({error})")
            pending = []
        rolled = False
        for path in pending:
            try:
                busctl("call", *NM, "CheckpointRollback", "o", path)
                rolled = True
            except BusctlFailed as error:
                print(f"the rollback failed ({error})")
        if rolled:
            print("rolled back what the join left")
            deadline = time.monotonic() + trusted_seconds("TM_NETWORK_RETURN_WAIT", RETURN_WAIT)
            while self.nm.device(self.device)[0] != CONNECTED and time.monotonic() < deadline:
                time.sleep(0.5)
        if state.get("saved") is False and valid_uuid(state.get("uuid")):
            status, _ = self.nm.call("connection", "delete", "uuid", state["uuid"])
            if status not in (0, 10):
                raise NmcliFailed(self.nm.last_error)

    def restart(self):
        """`connection up` on the active profile, tried once more when it fails, so the radio isn't left on nothing.
        The second failure still counts when the device ends up on the hotspot."""
        nm = self.nm
        self.step = "restart the hotspot"
        up = ("--wait", str(UP_WAIT), "connection", "up", "id", self.profile)
        status, _ = nm.call(*up, timeout=UP_WAIT + 30)
        if status != 0:
            print("the restart failed; trying once more")
            status, _ = nm.call(*up, timeout=UP_WAIT + 30)
            if status != 0:
                error = nm.last_error
                if nm.device(self.device) != (CONNECTED, self.profile):
                    raise NmcliFailed(error)
        print("restarted the hotspot")

    def turn_on(self):
        """Switch the radio on if it is off, and start the hotspot if the radio is idle."""
        nm = self.nm
        self.step = "switch the radio on"
        if nm.run("radio", "wifi").strip() != "enabled":
            nm.run("radio", "wifi", "on")
            print("switched the radio on")
        state, connection = nm.device(self.device)
        if connection is not None or state in JOINING:
            print("turned the hotspot on" if connection == self.profile
                  else "turned the hotspot on; it starts when the Wi-Fi leaves its network")
            return
        self.step = "start the hotspot"
        status, _ = nm.call("--wait", str(UP_WAIT), "connection", "up", "id", self.profile, timeout=UP_WAIT + 30)
        if status != 0:
            # NetworkManager may have started the hotspot by itself when autoconnect went on, and failed this start
            error = nm.last_error
            deadline = time.monotonic() + UP_WAIT
            while nm.device(self.device) != (CONNECTED, self.profile):
                if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                    raise NmcliFailed(error)
                time.sleep(0.5)
        print("turned the hotspot on")


def saved_note(run):
    """What a refusal or failure adds once the run has changed something."""
    return run.saved_note if run is not None and run.saved else ""


def main(argv):
    directory, request_name = os.path.split(argv[1] if len(argv) > 1 else REQUEST)
    jobs_fd = lock_fd = None
    nm = Nmcli(trusted("NMCLI", NMCLI))
    run = None
    step = "check the request"
    try:
        owner_uid, device, profile = read_manifest(manifest_path())
        jobs_fd = open_jobs_dir(directory or ".", owner_uid)
        action, values = check(read_request(jobs_fd, request_name, owner_uid))
        nm.hide(values.get("password"))
        if action in ("switch-now", "cancel"):  # never wait for the lock, which a join holds through its run
            run = Run(nm, device, profile)
            if action == "switch-now":
                run.switch_now()
            else:
                run.cancel()
            return 0
        step = "take the lock"
        lock_fd = take_lock(trusted("TM_NETWORK_LOCK", LOCK), trusted_seconds("TM_NETWORK_LOCK_WAIT", LOCK_WAIT))
        run = Run(nm, device, profile)
        if action == "hotspot":
            run.hotspot(values)
        elif action == "scan":
            run.scan()
        elif action == "forget":
            run.forget(values["uuid"])
        else:
            run.order(values["uuids"])
    except Refused as error:
        print(nm.scrub(f"refused: {error}{saved_note(run)}"))
        return 1
    except NmcliFailed as error:
        print(nm.scrub(f"failed: {run.step if run else step} ({error}){saved_note(run)}"))
        return 1
    except Exception as error:  # a message could quote the request, so print only the kind of error
        print(f"failed: {run.step if run else step} ({type(error).__name__}){saved_note(run)}")
        return 1
    finally:
        if run is not None and run.secrets_fd is not None:
            os.close(run.secrets_fd)
        if lock_fd is not None:
            os.close(lock_fd)
        if jobs_fd is not None:
            delete_request(jobs_fd, request_name)
            os.close(jobs_fd)
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))
